{"subject": "maths", "level": "ibdp", "topic_display": "Vectors (HL)", "topic_slug": "vectors-hl", "theme": "maths-grid", "adventure_n": 3, "title": "Lines, Planes and Distances", "emoji": "🛩️", "welcome_lead": "Equations of lines and planes in 3D, plus the distances between them.", "meta_desc": "HL Maths adventure on vector equations of lines, planes and distance formulas.", "final_note": "Line: r = a + λb; plane: r·n = d. Vectors rule 3D!", "concepts": [{"term": "Line equation", "def": "r = a + λb, point a, direction b."}, {"term": "Plane (vector)", "def": "r·n = d, n is the normal vector."}, {"term": "Plane (cartesian)", "def": "n1 x + n2 y + n3 z = d."}, {"term": "Point to plane", "def": "Distance = |n·p - d| / |n|."}, {"term": "Skew lines", "def": "Non-parallel lines that do not intersect."}, {"term": "Direction vector", "def": "Vector along the line's direction."}], "walkthroughs": [{"tag": "line", "h2": "Line Through Two Points", "body_html": "<p>Through A(1,2,3) and B(4,6,7).</p><p>Direction b = B - A = (3,4,4). So r = (1,2,3) + λ(3,4,4).</p>"}, {"tag": "plane", "h2": "Plane from Normal", "body_html": "<p>Plane through (1,1,1) with normal (2,3,1).</p><p>r·(2,3,1) = 2+3+1 = 6, so 2x + 3y + z = 6.</p>"}, {"tag": "dist", "h2": "Distance Point to Plane", "body_html": "<p>Distance from (0,0,0) to 2x + 3y + z = 6.</p><p>= |0 - 6| / √(4+9+1) = 6/√14 ≈ 1.60.</p>"}], "mcqs": [{"q": "Vector equation of a line?", "options": [["r = a + λb", 1], ["r·n = d", 0], ["ax + by = c", 0], ["r = a × b", 0]]}, {"q": "What does n represent for a plane?", "options": [["normal vector", 1], ["point on plane", 0], ["distance", 0], ["direction along plane", 0]]}], "numericals": [{"q": "Distance from origin to x + y + z = √3 (use |d|/|n|)?", "options": [0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0], "answer": 1.0}], "free_texts": [{"q": "Vector perpendicular to a plane?", "answer": "normal"}]}